<!--Post: 8111--><!--Time: 1108880554-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8111"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 19, 2005 - 10:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Since January 8th this case has been getting a LOT of attention from the kansas.com message board for various reasons.  I&#39;m making a post of it here to generate any &#34;no way&#34; or &#34;maybe looks interesting&#34; responses and to try to dig up any clues. <BR> <BR>Here is the first post that led to a long discussion:   <BR> <BR>&#34;case? This was a WSU student who was reported missing for several months during the time the Otero&#39;s were murdered. He was found in the trunk of his red mustang w/black hardtop, that was found in a very secluded rural area northeast of Wichita. The heavy snows of that winter hid his vehicle that was parked in a ravine on private property N.E. of Heights High. The cause of death was asphyxiation. The engine was left running, and he was found in the trunk of his mustang, with the trunk lid shut. The investigation concluded that it was an accidental suicide. Ever heard of that before? No suicide note was found. Our family knew this young man prior to his enrollment at WSU. He was our paperboy. Just the nicest clean cut outgoing kid you ever met. He always stopped for a few minutes to join in a yard football game, or to pet a barking dog that was fenced in. The reason I bring it up, is because video file footage of his car being found and investigators examining the vehicle, have been on CBS w/Dan Rather, and CBS Wichita affiliate station channel 12 news, that was reporting on the BTK case with video footage of the Otero&#39;s being wheeled out on gurnies after they were murdered. Coincidence? Video footage mixup? If anybody knows specifics about this case, I would be interested in hearing about it. Suicide??? Accidental suicide? I don&#39;t buy it for a moment.&#34; <BR> <BR>Is there any more information on this case?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8111-->
<!--Post: 8112--><!--Time: 1108880933-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8112"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 19, 2005 - 10:28 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Taken from here:  <a href="http://forums.prospero.com/n/mb/message.asp?webtag=kr-kansas_news&amp;msg=5105.1" target=_top>http://forums.prospero.com/n/mb/message.asp?webtag =kr-kansas_news&amp;msg=5105.1</a> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8112-->
<!--Post: 8178--><!--Time: 1108956382-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8178"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 20, 2005 - 7:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This would not be the first time that an early SK murder was initially thought to be suicide.  In particular, an early victim of Mike Ross was thought by LE for a long time to be a suicide, despite the loud protests of everybody who knew the victim.  This one stinks almost as badly.  The bottom line in both cases is that LE acted on the best available information at the time - but at that time, there was not a known SK to pin it on. <BR> <BR>I&#39;d like to know if the case records or photos would allow for the possibility that apparent attempted escape injuries might have either been, or masked, defensive injuries.  Decomposition was bad, but maybe there was something left.  Possibly too late for easy DNA, but who knows.  Justice is better late than never. <BR> <BR>Motive that might connect it to BTK?  Hard to say.  I&#39;ll leave that for somebody else.  But it wouldn&#39;t be unreasonable to think that a random killer might also kill somebody else for whom he had a reason.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8178-->
<!--Post: 8521--><!--Time: 1109183271-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8521"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Armchairpi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Armchairpi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 10:27 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I would like to add this case to my <a href="http://www.geocities.com/armchairpi/btk.htm">timeline</a> but can&#39;t find any news reporting of it on the web, or even on what date this occurred.  Anyone know where I can find something?  &#40;I don&#39;t have time to wade through all the messages at the AMW forum looking for the date, heh.  Tried already, and gave up after about three pages.&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8521-->
<!--Post: 8532--><!--Time: 1109186905-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8532"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iq<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iq<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 11:28 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Armchair- <BR> <BR>He was reported missing in November 1973 and he was found in the trunk of his car on January 21st 1974 &#40;6 days after the Otero killings&#41;.  <BR> <BR>Here is a link to a discussion with much more information: <BR><a href="http://forums.prospero.com/n/mb/message.asp?webtag=kr-kansas_news&amp;msg=5105.1" target=_top>http://forums.prospero.com/n/mb/message.asp?webtag =kr-kansas_news&amp;msg=5105.1</a> <BR> <BR>iq<!--/Text--></td></tr>
